        "problem": "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=1-{t}^{2},\\,\\,\\,y=3t+2,\\,-2\\le t\\le 2,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $a$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $b$ | $5$ | $8$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$",
        "worked_solution": "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=1-(-1)^{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y=3t+2.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=3(0)+2=2.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=1-(2)^{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0+2+(-3)=-1.\n$$",
